4:["$","article",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500","children":[["$","$L8",null,{"className":"transition hover:text-cyan-200","href":"/","children":"Home"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","$L8",null,{"className":"transition hover:text-cyan-200","href":"/blog","children":"Blog"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-slate-300","children":"What Is a Proforma Invoice? Meaning, Format & Sample"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-2","children":[["$","span","Proforma Invoice",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"Proforma Invoice"}],["$","span","Business Documents",{"className":"rounded-full bg-white/8 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-cyan-200","children":"Business Documents"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl","children":"What Is a Proforma Invoice? Meaning, Format & Sample"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300","children":"Learn proforma invoice meaning, format, sample, examples, PDF use cases, GST notes and how it differs from invoices and quotations."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500","children":["26 May 2026"," · ",13," min read · ","InvoiceWala Team"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-10","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-invert max-w-none prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-cyan-300","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"# What Is a Proforma Invoice? Meaning, Format & Sample"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"A proforma invoice is a preliminary invoice shared before the final sale happens. It looks similar to a normal invoice, but its purpose is different. A normal invoice is usually a request for payment after goods are supplied, services are completed, or a billing milestone is reached. A proforma invoice is shared earlier, often to show the buyer what the final invoice may look like if they approve the order."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Indian freelancers, exporters, agencies, contractors, manufacturers and service businesses use proforma invoices when the customer needs pricing confirmation before placing an order. It is useful when the buyer wants internal approval, the seller needs advance payment, the order is customized, or shipment/export documentation needs an estimated commercial value."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The simplest way to understand it: a proforma invoice is a draft commercial document. It lists the expected products or services, quantity, rate, tax estimate, total amount, delivery terms and payment terms. It gives clarity before the final invoice is created."}]]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"This guide explains proforma invoice meaning, format, sample, GST notes, examples, common mistakes and how it differs from quotations, estimates and tax invoices."}]]}],["$","h2","5",{"className":"mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-white","children":"Quick Answer"}],["$","p","6",{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300","children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"A proforma invoice is a preliminary bill issued before the final invoice. It is used to confirm price, product/service details, taxes, payment terms and delivery terms before the actual sale is completed."}]]}],"$La","$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$